## What the code does

`crate-jmap-metadata-client/src/methods/metadata.rs:68-72` serialises the `properties: Option<&[&str]>` argument to a JSON array via a hand-rolled iterator chain:

```rust
if let Some(props) = properties {
    args["properties"] = serde_json::Value::Array(
        props.iter().copied().map(serde_json::Value::from).collect(),
    );
}
```

## What idiomatic Rust would do

`serde_json::to_value` on `&[&str]` invokes the `str` Serialize impl on each element and produces `Value::Array(Vec<Value::String>)` — byte-identical wire output to the hand-rolled version:

```rust
if let Some(props) = properties {
    args["properties"] = serde_json::to_value(props)
        .expect("&[&str] Serialize is infallible");
}
```

…matches the idiom the SAME function uses three lines above for the `ids` slice (metadata.rs:65-67):

```rust
if let Some(id_slice) = ids {
    args["ids"] = serde_json::to_value(id_slice).expect("Id slice Serialize is infallible");
}
```

## What goes wrong if it stays

Nothing at runtime — both forms produce the same wire JSON. The cost is *clarity and internal consistency*: the same function performs the same kind of operation (slice-to-JSON-array) two different ways, three lines apart. A reader has to parse the iterator chain and convince themselves it produces the same shape as a one-line `to_value` would.

## Workspace propagation footprint

This is **NOT a metadata-client divergence from canonical mail-client** — `crate-jmap-mail-client/src/methods/email.rs:44-48` has the IDENTICAL hand-rolled pattern. Both the canonical and metadata-client cookie-cut sibling share the regression. JMAP-1j9k.20 (open) already tracks the same pattern across all 6 sites in calendars-client. The right fix path is workspace-wide:

1. Fix canonical `jmap-mail-client/src/methods/email.rs:44-48` first.
2. Propagate to every extension-client sibling (calendars, contacts, chat, tasks, filenode, sharing, metadata) in the same pass.
3. Per workspace AGENTS.md "Canonical Templates" rule.

Cross-reference: JMAP-1j9k.20 (calendars-client, same pattern, open).

## Scope

`crate-jmap-metadata-client/src/methods/metadata.rs:68-72` (one site).
